@startuml seq_sft_overspeed_refused
title SC-SFT-05 - Downshift refused by the overspeed protection

actor "Console user" as User
participant "Console" as Console
participant "Plant model" as Plant
participant "TCU" as TCU

note over User, TCU
Covers: SYS-SFT-005, SYS-SFT-003, SYS-SFT-001, SG-02
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04.
Ratios 1st 3.06, 2nd 1.63 (system_context section 4.1); downshift speed limit 6000 rpm.
end note

note over TCU: D in 2nd at 100 km/h, mode Normal
User -> Console : kick-down, throttle 100 %
Console -> Plant : Throttle = 100 %
Plant -> TCU : SIM_Driver: Throttle = 100 %; SIM_Speed: InputShaftSpeed, OutputShaftSpeed
TCU -> TCU : downshift table gives target gear 1 (SYS-SFT-001)
TCU -> TCU : prediction for 1st = max(OutputShaftSpeed x 3.06,\nInputShaftSpeed x 3.06 / 1.63) = about 8460 rpm > 6000 rpm
TCU -> TCU : downshift 2 -> 1 not started, 2nd kept (SYS-SFT-005)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: SS_A = OFF, SS_B = ON (2nd unchanged)
note over Plant, TCU: Safe state of SG-02: the current gear is kept.

opt OutputShaftSpeed frozen while InputShaftSpeed is valid
  TCU -> TCU : the InputShaftSpeed term still gives > 6000 rpm -> refused\n(SYS-SFT-005 verification)
end

loop while the prediction for 1st is > 6000 rpm
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Speed: speeds (vehicle slows down)
  TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: SS_A = OFF, SS_B = ON (2nd)
end
... prediction for 1st <= 6000 rpm ...
TCU -> TCU : downshift 2 -> 1 may start (target still 1, SYS-SFT-004 elapsed)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: SS_A = ON, SS_B = ON (1st), shift pressure profile
Plant -> Plant : ratio 1.63 -> 3.06 over 400 ms (SIM-PLT-003)
@enduml
